{"type":"message","id":"16b53282","parentId":"e03f06be","timestamp":"2026-04-14T19:11:40.024Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have enough context. Let me:\n\n1. Check tasks for staleness (>60 min since updated_at vs now)\n2. Update heartbeat\n3. Update the shared pool progress doc\n\nCurrent timestamp: 1776193889 (UTC seconds)\n\nLet me convert some key task timestamps:\n- \"任务监督与检查\" - d91e9834 - updated_at: 1774826680144 = April 7, 2026 (months old, definitely stale)\n\nLet me look at more recent tasks and their updated_at times to find any that might be >60 min stale.\n\nActually, let me look at the current time vs updated_at more carefully. The current timestamp is 1776193889. \n\n\nNow I'm checking which tasks haven't been updated in over 60 minutes by comparing their updated_at timestamps to the current time.\n\nLooking through the task list, all of these updated_at values are significantly older than 60 minutes - they range from months to years in the past, so they're all stale and should be marked accordingly. Looking at the remaining tasks with the same staleness pattern - they're all significantly overdue by months. The real issue here is that most of these tasks lack proper due dates and were created without clear deadlines, so they're lingering indefinitely rather than being genuinely active work items. I should mark them as stale and then update the progress documentation.\n\nNow I'm pulling up the bitable to record this progress report."},{"type":"text","text":"Now let me check the bitable (progress repository) and update heartbeat:\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_kds8hiav51od_1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"~/workspace/agent/workspace/skills/shared-pool/SKILL.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_function_kds8hiav51od_2","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"cat ~/workspace/agent/workspace/memory/heartbeat-state.json 2>/dev/null || echo \"No heartbeat state file\""}}],"api":"openai-completi